one-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-20T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Broomfield, CO; Douglas, CO; Denver, CO; Weld, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T09:54:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 200954 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 354 AM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Warmer and drier conditions expected today, with isolated showers/storms in the mountains. - Slight increase in afternoon showers/storms on Friday, with a few capable of producing gusty outflows. - Monsoon moisture returns this weekend and holds into early","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T10:13:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... Mostly dry and hot conditions are expected today, with only isolated showers/storms possible in the mountains of Park County. North and Middle Park will see RH drop into the mid teens this afternoon while the majority of the lower elevations stay above 15%. Winds are expected to generally remain light, with North Park seeing gusts up to 20 mph. Overnight recoveri","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"gby01","station_name":"Granby","distance_km":37.2,"soil_temp_5cm_f":49.96,"soil_temp_15cm_f":61.47,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soi